# {repo_name} ({package_name})

## General notes

- Do not include "Co-Authored-By" in commit messages.
- Assume `CASM_PREFIX` is already set in the environment.

## Available tools and skills

- MCP server `superchivo` — search Python package docs
- `/casm` — CASM suite overview and common workflow patterns
- `/casm-version` — Version update checklist
- `/casm-release` — Release procedure

## Development workflow

**Before testing new code, always install the package:**

    pip install -v --no-build-isolation .

This is required because the package has C++ extensions (pybind11 bindings). Without it, `pytest` will fail with `AttributeError` or `ImportError` on the compiled modules.

**Run all Python tests:**

    pytest -rsap -x python/tests

**Format Python files:**

    black python
    ruff check --fix python

**Format C++ files (staged only):**

    ./stylize.sh

**After adding new source files, update CMakeLists.txt:**

    python make_CMakeLists.py

**Update `CHANGELOG.md` when making commits.**

## C++ tests

```bash
# Uninstall the Python package so its C++ library isn't used during testing
pip uninstall {package_name}

# Build and install the C++ library
cmake -B build_cxx_only -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release && cmake --build build_cxx_only -j$(getconf _NPROCESSORS_ONLN 2>/dev/null || sysctl -n hw.ncpu) --verbose && cmake --install build_cxx_only

# Build and run C++ tests
cmake -B build_cxx_test -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release tests && cmake --build build_cxx_test -j$(getconf _NPROCESSORS_ONLN 2>/dev/null || sysctl -n hw.ncpu) --verbose && ctest --test-dir build_cxx_test
# Log: build_cxx_test/Testing/Temporary/LastTest.log

# Uninstall the C++ library when done
xargs rm < build_cxx_only/install_manifest.txt
```

